From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:42:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] Decode all-reduce consume: the wait for the peers
 folded into the norm kernel behind G6_AR_WAITFOLD=1|2

k_ar_wait_add_norm<W> (glue.cuh) runs k_ar_add_norm's loads, adds and stores in the same order after the wait
k_wait_peers did in a launch of its own: 1 = CTA 0 of each row cluster polls, then a cluster barrier; 2 = every CTA
polls (as k_qs_get). The target step's consumes only (the MTP draft step's keep the split pair: G6_DRAFT_PAR's
progress rule). k_ar_add_norm (W = 0) compiles to the same SASS as before. m4sim takes the flag too (byte A/B on one
GPU). kernels/tests/ar_fold_test.cu: byte equality of fold 1 / 2 vs the split pair with ready and late tails, and the
per-consume time.
